# PX4 parameters this project depends on, one "NAME VALUE" per line.
#
# Copied unchanged from quad-autonomy-sim, which found each of these the hard
# way. scripts/sim.sh applies them to every agent at every boot: as
# PX4_PARAM_* env vars early in boot, then again with
# `px4-param --instance N set` once boot finishes (see sim.sh for why twice).
#
# Only list parameters we actually rely on, each with the reason. Anything not
# here is the airframe default for gz_x500_flow (SYS_AUTOSTART 4021).

# Offboard: fall out of offboard if no setpoint for 1 s (the node streams at 20 Hz).
COM_OF_LOSS_T 1.0
# Offboard-loss action: 5 = Hold mode (hover in place). The node never re-engages on its own.
COM_OBL_RC_ACT 5
# Auto-disarm 2 s after landing; the node treats "disarmed" as mission complete.
COM_DISARM_LAND 2.0
# DDS domain the uXRCE-DDS client joins; must match ROS_DOMAIN_ID on the ROS 2 side.
UXRCE_DDS_DOM_ID 0

# IMU integration rate for vehicle_imu -> sensor_combined (Hz). Default 250 Hz
# in SITL, but the uXRCE-DDS client forwards sensor_combined at ~100 Hz and
# sends only the latest sample, so ~60% of IMU intervals never reached ROS 2
# (4 ms integrals arriving every ~10 ms). At 100 Hz each message covers its whole
# interval. EKF2 predicts at 100 Hz anyway (EKF2_PREDICT_US), and rate/attitude
# control uses vehicle_angular_velocity, which this does not affect.
IMU_INTEG_RATE 100
